{
  "_comment": [
    "The only version numbers a human edits, per doc/Alignment.md §2.",
    "",
    "Nothing derives from this file yet: the shared changelog engine is §3's",
    "item and its location is explicitly open, so vendoring a fourth copy of",
    "changelog.py here would be the exact drift §3 exists to end. What does",
    "read it today is scripts/check-version.mjs, which holds this file, ",
    "package.json, src/version.js and index.html's two copies to one number.",
    "",
    "TECHNO_CHANGELOG is written for the engine that does not exist yet, in",
    "the shape §3 specifies, so adopting it is a delete-the-comment change."
  ],

  "TECHNO_VERSION": {
    "major": 0,
    "minor": 13,
    "patch": 0,
    "pre": null
  },

  "TECHNO_CHANGELOG": {
    "project": "Diluvium Lab",
    "intro_extra": "\nThe Lab versions independently of Diluvium. The coupling is RECORDED,\nnot required: every entry names the Diluvium revision the page bundles\nin `vendor/`, so \"which Diluvium is inside\" is a fact you read off the\nrelease rather than a tag-naming convention. The Lab also *runs* builds\nit does not bundle, chosen from the release mirror at run time, so its\nown version could never have named one of them.\n",

    "facts": [
      {
        "id": "dil",
        "keys": ["diluvium", "diluvium_build"],
        "fmt": "diluvium `{diluvium!s:.12}` (build{diluvium_build})"
      },
      {
        "id": "dil",
        "keys": ["diluvium"],
        "fmt": "diluvium `{diluvium!s:.12}`"
      },
      {
        "id": "nbformat",
        "keys": ["nbformat"],
        "fmt": "nbformat {nbformat}"
      }
    ],

    "tag_rule": "exact",
    "required": ["version", "tag", "status", "stable", "mirror", "summary"],
    "emit_json": true,

    "stamps": [
      {
        "file": "package.json",
        "find": "\"version\":\\s*\"([0-9A-Za-z.+-]+)\"",
        "spelling": "semver"
      },
      {
        "file": "src/version.js",
        "find": "export const LAB_VERSION = '([0-9A-Za-z.+-]+)'",
        "spelling": "semver"
      },
      {
        "file": "index.html",
        "find": "<meta name=\"diluvium-lab-build\" content=\"([0-9A-Za-z.+-]+)\"",
        "spelling": "semver"
      },
      {
        "file": "index.html",
        "find": "var EXPECTED = '([0-9A-Za-z.+-]+)'",
        "spelling": "semver"
      },
      {
        "file": "package-lock.json",
        "find": "^  \"version\": \"([0-9A-Za-z.+-]+)\"",
        "spelling": "semver"
      },
      {
        "file": "index.html",
        "find": "\\?v=([0-9A-Za-z.+-]+)\"",
        "spelling": "semver"
      }
    ],

    "_stamps_note": [
      "The engine runs each `find` with re.findall and requires EVERY match",
      "to agree, so the import map is one stamp covering all 50 stamped",
      "module URLs rather than something stamps cannot express.",
      "",
      "package-lock.json names this package twice: the top-level `version`",
      "at two-space indent, and packages[\"\"].version at six -- where every",
      "dependency's version also lives. One pattern cannot select the second",
      "without also demanding that @playwright/test be 0.13.0, so the stamp",
      "takes the top-level copy and scripts/check-version.mjs takes the",
      "other. It had already drifted: the lock sat at 0.11.0 through the",
      "whole of 0.12.0 and nothing noticed.",
      "",
      "`spelling` is `semver` here and that is a statement of intent rather",
      "than a working value for a prerelease. Measured against technoproj",
      "v0.1.0: `semver` and `base` both resolve to the base X.Y.Z with the",
      "prerelease stripped, and the only spelling that yields the tag body",
      "`0.14.0-rc.1` is the one named `pep440` -- which per ALIGNMENT §1 is",
      "the derived spelling and would be `0.14.0rc1`. Every file stamped",
      "here holds the tag body, because LAB_VERSION is what the stale-scripts",
      "banner compares. So on the Lab's first prerelease these four stamps",
      "want 0.14.0 and the tree says 0.14.0-rc.1, until the engine grows a",
      "tag-body spelling. See ROADMAP; `pep440` is the stopgap if it is",
      "needed before then."
    ]
  },

  "TECHNO_INIT_DIRS": [
    ".nogit",
    ".dump",
    "scripts"
  ],

  "TECHNO_COPYRIGHT": "Copyright Michael Godfrey [2026] | aloecraft.org [michael@aloecraft.org]"
}
